[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986518-1200256842.gif[/img][/center]

[url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]Fallout Chat Mod[/url] brings real-time community chat to Fallout 76 with a Pip-Boy-styled interface. Coordinate events, find trading partners, organize parties, and send private messages without switching away from your game.

Choose how you want to use it:
[list]
[*][b]Desktop overlay:[/b] A transparent, draggable, resizable chat window that runs outside Fallout 76. Available for Windows and Linux.[/*]
[*][b]Optional in-game HUD mod:[/b] Display chat directly inside the game with HUDModLoader and either ZFE or xScal. One HUD download supports both extenders.[/*]
[/list]

The desktop overlay does not modify game files, read game memory, inject code, or scan networks or ports. It checks whether the Fallout76 process is running to show or hide the overlay. No script extender is required for the desktop overlay.

The optional HUD mod is a separate, explicit modding install. It loads UI assets through HUDModLoader and uses the installed extender's supported chat interface. Server chat uses data the game exposes to its own HUD. HUD compatibility may require updates after game or extender patches.

Visit [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]falloutchatmod.com[/url] for downloads, installation instructions, and support.

[b][size=4]Code Signing and Virus Scanning[/size][/b]

The Windows installer is digitally signed. Desktop releases must pass a packaged startup smoke test and a completed VirusTotal scan before publication. The v1.3.100 Windows release scan reported zero malicious and zero suspicious detections.

View the current Windows release scan: [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/virustotal]VirusTotal results[/url].

[b][size=4]Main Features[/size][/b]

[b]Community channels[/b]
Chat in General, Trading, Events, Infests, and Raids. Use channel tabs or shortcuts to find the conversation you need.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986682-344970336.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Private messages[/b]
Send private messages directly to other users, with conversation history and unread indicators. Public @mentions stay in public chat; they do not become private messages.

[b]Parties[/b]
Create and join parties, invite other players, and coordinate in private party conversations.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986698-180659483.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Discord bridge[/b]
Supported community channels connect to Discord, allowing conversations to continue between the app and the community server. Private messages remain private conversations between their participants.

[b]Steam or Discord sign-in[/b]
Create or link your account using Steam or Discord. Steam sign-in does not require a Discord account. Leave your name blank to use your Steam display name, and link Discord later from your profile if you wish.

[b]Optional HUD server chat[/b]
The HUD's SERVER channel becomes available after your current world is confirmed. SERVER messages also appear in General for users mapped to that same server, with a SERVER label. The world binding clears when you leave and is established again when you join another world.

[b]Emojis and GIFs[/b]
The desktop chat supports rich messages, emojis, and GIFs. The HUD presents a text feed: custom Discord emojis appear as readable :name: labels, and image/GIF attachments are not displayed there.

[b]Wiki and reference tools[/b]
Look up game information and camp resources from the overlay.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986806-1247131354.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Commands and giveaways[/b]
Use commands for common activities and reference information. Giveaway commands include /giveawaystart and /giveawaylist where available to your account.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/2590/images/4082/4082-1780986668-546220891.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Appearance and moderation[/b]
Customize the chat's appearance and explore supporter cosmetics. Report messages and bugs through the app; moderation tools help keep community channels usable.

[b]Manual updates[/b]
The desktop app notifies you when an update is available. Download and install updates yourself; the app does not automatically download or install them.

[b][size=4]What's New in v1.3.100[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed private-message routing so public @mentions do not appear in PM history.[/*]
[*]Improved private-message conversations and unread handling.[/*]
[*]Added Steam alongside Discord for account sign-in and HUD linking.[/*]
[*]Use your Steam display name when you leave your name blank.[/*]
[*]Link Discord later from your profile.[/*]
[*]Improved HUD message delivery and history recovery across server leaves and joins.[/*]
[*]Show same-server SERVER messages in General as well as the SERVER channel.[/*]
[*]Improved HUD input handoff and channel navigation with ZFE and xScal.[/*]
[*]Unified the HUD download: one auto-detecting BA2 with examples for both extenders.[/*]
[*]Included xScal chat setup helpers and complete manual installation instructions.[/*]
[/list]

[b][size=4]Requirements — Desktop Overlay[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Fallout 76 on PC.[/*]
[*]64-bit Windows 10/11 or Linux.[/*]
[*]An internet connection and a Steam or Discord account. Discord sign-in requires membership in the community Discord.[/*]
[*]Borderless Windowed mode. Linux users should also follow the compositor/window instructions included with their download.[/*]
[/list]
A script extender and the optional HUD mod are not required for the desktop overlay.

[b][size=4]Desktop Overlay Installation[/size][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download the package for your operating system.[/*]
[*]Windows: extract the installer ZIP and run Fallout Chat Mod Setup. This is a per-user installation. Linux: use the AppImage or install the .deb package, following the included instructions.[/*]
[*]Launch Fallout Chat Mod and sign in with Steam or Discord.[/*]
[*]Complete onboarding. Leave your name blank to use your Steam display name when signing in with Steam.[/*]
[*]Run Fallout 76 in Borderless Windowed mode and position the overlay where you want it.[/*]
[*]Use Insert to interact with chat and Delete to toggle overlay visibility. Page Up/Page Down switch channels. Check Settings for your configured shortcuts.[/*]
[/list]
For updates, download the new package and install it manually. Your settings are stored separately from the application files.

[b][size=4]Optional In-Game HUD Mod — One Download for ZFE and xScal[/size][/b]

The FCM HUD Mod ZIP contains [b]one FCMChatWidget.ba2[/b] that automatically detects the installed extender. It includes configuration examples for both ZFE and xScal; apply only the one for your setup.

The desktop application is not required for HUD chat. The HUD is a text chat interface and does not include every desktop feature.

You need HUDModLoader, one compatible extender (ZFE with chat.v1 support or xScal with chatInterface support), the FCM HUD Mod ZIP, an internet connection, and a linked account.

[b][size=4]Manual HUD Installation — No Installer Required[/size][/b]

You can install and configure the HUD entirely by hand. The included xScal setup helper is optional; the manual settings are listed below.

[b]1. Close the game and install the dependencies[/b]

Exit Fallout 76 completely. Install HUDModLoader and your chosen extender using their authors' instructions.

Open your Fallout 76 installation folder. This is the folder containing Fallout76.exe and the Data folder.

[b]2. Extract the HUD files[/b]

Extract the FCM HUD Mod ZIP into the Fallout 76 installation folder, preserving its folder structure.

The shared HUD files should be at:
[code]
Fallout76/
  Fallout76.exe
  Data/
    FCMChatWidget.ba2
    FCMChat.ini
[/code]

The ZIP also includes the HUDModLoader append snippet, Fallout76Custom.ini.example, examples/ZFE/FCMChatWidget.ini.example, xscal.ini.example, optional xScal setup helpers, and INSTALL.txt.

[b]3. Register the widget with HUDModLoader[/b]

Back up and open Data/hudmodloader.ini. Append the following line exactly once, keeping all existing widget entries:
[code]
FCMChatWidget
[/code]
Do not replace your existing hudmodloader.ini with the included snippet.

[b]4. Register the BA2 archive[/b]

Back up and open Fallout76Custom.ini.

Windows normally stores it in Documents/My Games/Fallout 76/.
For Steam Proton, open steamapps/compatdata/1151340/pfx/drive_c/users/steamuser/, then Documents/My Games/Fallout 76/.

In the existing [Archive] section, append FCMChatWidget.ba2 to the comma-separated sResourceArchive2List value. Keep all existing archives, including HUDModLoader.

A minimal example is:
[code]
[Archive]
sResourceArchive2List=HUDModLoader.ba2,FCMChatWidget.ba2
[/code]
Add a missing section or key once. Do not create duplicate [Archive] sections or replace your existing archive list.

[b]5. Configure your chosen extender[/b]

Follow one of the sections below.

[b]Manual xScal Configuration[/b]

Back up and open xscal.ini beside Fallout76.exe. Edit the existing [Chat] section to use:
[code]
[Chat]
enabled=true
relayEndpoint=wss://falloutchatmod.com/relay
[/code]
[list]
[*]Change enabled=false to enabled=true and replace the relayEndpoint value with the one above.[/*]
[*]If [Chat] is missing, add the section once.[/*]
[*]If xscal.ini is missing, create a plain-text file named xscal.ini beside Fallout76.exe. Make sure it is not named xscal.ini.txt.[/*]
[*]Preserve unrelated settings. Do not add duplicate sections or keys.[/*]
[*]xScal does not use the ZFE fragment. Do not create ZFE folders for an xScal installation.[/*]
[/list]

[b]New users must apply these settings too.[/b] xScal ships with chat disabled by default. Extracting xscal.ini.example alone does not activate it.

On Windows, you can optionally run Enable-xScal-Chat.cmd instead of editing the configuration by hand. The helper backs up the configuration and preserves unrelated settings.

Restart Fallout 76 after changing the configuration.

[b]Manual ZFE Configuration[/b]

Copy the complete file:
[code]
examples/ZFE/FCMChatWidget.ini.example
[/code]
to:
[code]
Data/ZFE/TextChat/fragments/FCMChatWidget.ini
[/code]

Create the folders if needed and remove the .example suffix. Back up any existing fragment and compare its settings before replacing it.

The production example includes:
[code]
Endpoint=wss://falloutchatmod.com/relay
[/code]
[b]Copy the complete example, not just the Endpoint line.[/b]

Keep OpenChatKey aligned with openKey in Data/FCMChat.ini and any override in Data/configuration/zfe.ini. ZFE does not need xscal.ini.

Restart Fallout 76 after changing the configuration.

[b]6. Verify the HUD and link your account[/b]

Start Fallout 76 and press F11 to open HUDModLoader. Confirm the FCM menu is present.

When the widget displays a fresh link code:
[list=1]
[*]Open [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/link]falloutchatmod.com/link[/url].[/*]
[*]Sign in with Steam or Discord.[/*]
[*]Enter the code shown in your HUD and return to the game.[/*]
[/list]
Steam sign-in does not require Discord. If you leave your name blank, your Steam display name is used. You can link Discord later from your profile.

Codes expire after 10 minutes. Reconnect the widget to request a new code if necessary.

[b][size=4]HUD Controls[/size][/b]
[list]
[*]Insert: open chat input.[/*]
[*]Enter: send. Escape: cancel.[/*]
[*]Page Up / Page Down: switch channels.[/*]
[*]Arrow Up / Down while typing: scroll the feed.[/*]
[*]Home / End while typing: return to the newest message.[/*]
[*]/g, /t, /e, /i, /r: send to General, Trading, Events, Infests, or Raids.[/*]
[*]/s or /server: send to SERVER after the current world is confirmed.[/*]
[*]/hide: hide the feed. Insert restores it.[/*]
[*]F11: open HUDModLoader settings and the FCM customization menu.[/*]
[/list]
Server detection may take time after joining a world. If users on the same world are mapped differently, please report it with your HUD version, extender, world type, and whether you recently changed servers.

[b][size=4]Roadmap[/size][/b]

Planned areas include clans, additional Fallout games (Fallout 3, New Vegas, and Fallout 4), trading integrations, and Nexus account linking. These are future plans, not current requirements or promised release dates.

Private messages, appearance customization, Steam/Discord linking, and optional HUD server chat are available now.

[b][size=4]Support and Bug Reports[/size][/b]

Use the Nexus Posts/Bugs tabs or the app's report tools, or join [url=https://discord.gg/NJBJqyvRJC]our Discord[/url]. Visit [url=https://falloutchatmod.com/]falloutchatmod.com[/url] for downloads and installation help.

Please include your operating system, version, and whether you use the desktop overlay or HUD. For HUD problems, include ZFE or xScal and its version. For server chat problems, include public/private world and whether you left or joined another world before the issue occurred.
